WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:00.794
Hooks on X:

2
00:00:00.794 --> 00:00:03.254
twenty opening lines that stop the scroll.

3
00:00:03.254 --> 00:00:07.412
In this video we'll go through each one,
with an example you can adapt.

4
00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:10.435
A hook is the opening line of your post.

5
00:00:10.435 --> 00:00:14.929
On X, the feed shows only the first lines
of a longer post before Show more.

6
00:00:14.929 --> 00:00:18.832
If those lines don't grab attention,
people simply keep scrolling.

7
00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.133
Here are all twenty at a glance.

8
00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:23.888
Each one triggers a different reason to
keep reading.

9
00:00:23.888 --> 00:00:25.292
Let's take them one by one.

10
00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.686
Number 1, the Curiosity Hook.

11
00:00:27.686 --> 00:00:28.404
For example:

12
00:00:28.404 --> 00:00:33.672
Nobody talks about this, but most viral
threads are rewritten five times before
posting.

13
00:00:33.672 --> 00:00:37.742
It opens a gap between what readers know
and what they want to know.

14
00:00:37.742 --> 00:00:40.975
Use it when you have a genuinely
lesser-known insight.

15
00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:43.586
Number 2, the Contrarian Hook.

16
00:00:43.586 --> 00:00:44.368
For example:

17
00:00:44.368 --> 00:00:45.541
Unpopular opinion:

18
00:00:45.541 --> 00:00:48.214
posting every day is hurting your growth.

19
00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.887
Disagreement makes people stop and react.

20
00:00:50.887 --> 00:00:54.212
Use it only for an opinion you can
actually defend.

21
00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.608
Number 3, the Negative Hook.

22
00:00:56.608 --> 00:00:57.353
For example:

23
00:00:57.353 --> 00:01:01.388
Stop ending your posts with "thoughts?" if
you want real replies.

24
00:01:01.388 --> 00:01:04.306
Fear of doing something wrong is a strong
pull.

25
00:01:04.306 --> 00:01:07.906
Name one specific habit, then show the
better alternative.

26
00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.277
Number 4, the Number Hook.

27
00:01:10.277 --> 00:01:11.074
For example:

28
00:01:11.074 --> 00:01:13.798
I made my first $1,000 from a newsletter.

29
00:01:13.798 --> 00:01:14.528
Here's how.

30
00:01:14.528 --> 00:01:17.783
Concrete results are believable and easy
to scan.

31
00:01:17.783 --> 00:01:20.307
Only use real numbers you can back up.

32
00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:22.643
Number 5, the Story Hook.

33
00:01:22.643 --> 00:01:23.456
For example:

34
00:01:23.456 --> 00:01:26.504
2 years ago, I was posting to zero
followers.

35
00:01:26.504 --> 00:01:30.974
A time jump promises a journey, and people
love to follow a story.

36
00:01:30.974 --> 00:01:33.615
Great for personal lessons and threads.

37
00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:36.007
Number 6, the Mistake Hook.

38
00:01:36.007 --> 00:01:36.779
For example:

39
00:01:36.779 --> 00:01:41.024
My biggest mistake as a freelancer was
saying yes to every client.

40
00:01:41.024 --> 00:01:45.784
Admitting a mistake builds trust, and
readers want to avoid the same pain.

41
00:01:45.784 --> 00:01:47.907
Use it to share hard-won lessons.

42
00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:50.335
Number 7, the Warning Hook.

43
00:01:50.335 --> 00:01:51.128
For example:

44
00:01:51.128 --> 00:01:53.773
Avoid this pricing mistake at all costs.

45
00:01:53.773 --> 00:01:56.021
It signals urgency and protection.

46
00:01:56.021 --> 00:02:00.450
Save it for mistakes that really are
costly, or it feels like hype.

47
00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:02.708
Number 8, the Secret Hook.

48
00:02:02.708 --> 00:02:03.445
For example:

49
00:02:03.445 --> 00:02:06.578
Here's what nobody tells you about going
freelance.

50
00:02:06.578 --> 00:02:08.422
It promises insider knowledge.

51
00:02:08.422 --> 00:02:12.784
Works best when you share the unglamorous
truth behind a popular topic.

52
00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:15.040
Number 9, the Proof Hook.

53
00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:15.812
For example:

54
00:02:15.812 --> 00:02:18.967
I went from 200 to 5,000 followers by
doing this.

55
00:02:18.967 --> 00:02:22.122
A clear before-and-after shows your advice
works.

56
00:02:22.122 --> 00:02:25.083
Lead with the result, then explain the
method.

57
00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:27.337
Number 10, the List Hook.

58
00:02:27.337 --> 00:02:28.118
For example:

59
00:02:28.118 --> 00:02:30.916
7 things I wish I knew before my first
job.

60
00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:35.276
A number tells readers exactly what they
get and how long it takes.

61
00:02:35.276 --> 00:02:36.578
Perfect for threads.

62
00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:39.003
Number 11, the How-To Hook.

63
00:02:39.003 --> 00:02:39.791
For example:

64
00:02:39.791 --> 00:02:42.615
How to grow on X without posting every
day.

65
00:02:42.615 --> 00:02:46.687
It promises a result while removing the
obstacle people dread.

66
00:02:46.687 --> 00:02:49.510
Use it for practical, step-by-step
content.

67
00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:52.208
Number 12, the Comparison Hook.

68
00:02:52.208 --> 00:02:53.005
For example:

69
00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:54.864
Most people chase followers.

70
00:02:54.864 --> 00:02:57.055
Smart people build relationships.

71
00:02:57.055 --> 00:03:00.641
Contrast makes readers ask which group
they belong to.

72
00:03:00.641 --> 00:03:02.832
Use it to reframe a common habit.

73
00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:05.346
Number 13, the Challenge Hook.

74
00:03:05.346 --> 00:03:06.096
For example:

75
00:03:06.096 --> 00:03:08.285
I wrote one post a day for 30 days.

76
00:03:08.285 --> 00:03:09.598
Here's what happened.

77
00:03:09.598 --> 00:03:12.787
It's a mini experiment with a built-in
cliffhanger.

78
00:03:12.787 --> 00:03:15.851
Share honest results, including what
didn't work.

79
00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:18.452
Number 14, the Prediction Hook.

80
00:03:18.452 --> 00:03:19.204
For example:

81
00:03:19.204 --> 00:03:22.273
AI agents are going to change how we shop
online.

82
00:03:22.273 --> 00:03:24.904
Bold predictions spark debate and replies.

83
00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:27.785
Back them with reasoning, not just
excitement.

84
00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:30.365
Number 15, the Relatable Hook.

85
00:03:30.365 --> 00:03:31.138
For example:

86
00:03:31.138 --> 00:03:34.427
If you're struggling to stay consistent,
read this.

87
00:03:34.427 --> 00:03:37.071
Readers feel seen and spoken to directly.

88
00:03:37.071 --> 00:03:39.973
Use it for supportive, problem-solving
posts.

89
00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:42.474
Number 16, the Direct Callout.

90
00:03:42.474 --> 00:03:43.211
For example:

91
00:03:43.211 --> 00:03:46.038
If you're a beginner in Web3, this is for
you.

92
00:03:46.038 --> 00:03:49.909
Calling out one audience makes the right
people stop scrolling.

93
00:03:49.909 --> 00:03:51.814
Be specific about who it's for.

94
00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:54.044
Number 17, the FOMO Hook.

95
00:03:54.044 --> 00:03:54.799
For example:

96
00:03:54.799 --> 00:03:58.513
You're missing out on replies if you're
not using X Spaces.

97
00:03:58.513 --> 00:04:00.779
Fear of missing out triggers action.

98
00:04:00.779 --> 00:04:03.737
Make sure the opportunity is real and
worth it.

99
00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:06.476
Number 18, the Myth-Busting Hook.

100
00:04:06.476 --> 00:04:07.235
For example:

101
00:04:07.235 --> 00:04:10.144
You don't need a big audience to land
clients.

102
00:04:10.144 --> 00:04:13.115
It removes a limiting belief and feels
freeing.

103
00:04:13.115 --> 00:04:16.466
Use it to challenge common assumptions in
your niche.

104
00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:19.375
Number 19, the Transformation Hook.

105
00:04:19.375 --> 00:04:20.152
For example:

106
00:04:20.152 --> 00:04:23.906
Here's how I went from burned out to
loving my work again.

107
00:04:23.906 --> 00:04:26.106
It sells change, not just numbers.

108
00:04:26.106 --> 00:04:29.731
Great for personal growth, career and
lifestyle stories.

109
00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.272
Number 20, the Open-Loop Hook.

110
00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:33.025
For example:

111
00:04:33.025 --> 00:04:36.162
I almost quit writing online, until this
happened.

112
00:04:36.162 --> 00:04:40.365
An unfinished story begs to be finished,
so people click Show more.

113
00:04:40.365 --> 00:04:42.184
Pay it off in the next lines.

114
00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:43.542
A few tips.

115
00:04:43.542 --> 00:04:45.030
Deliver on the promise:

116
00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:47.876
the rest of your post must pay off the
hook.

117
00:04:47.876 --> 00:04:51.176
Avoid clickbait, because overpromising
burns trust.

118
00:04:51.176 --> 00:04:53.181
Match the hook to your content.

119
00:04:53.181 --> 00:04:54.346
And test and vary:

120
00:04:54.346 --> 00:04:58.292
rotate different hooks and see what lands
with your audience.

121
00:04:58.950 --> 00:04:59.495
Remember:

122
00:04:59.495 --> 00:05:01.493
your first line is your headline.

123
00:05:01.493 --> 00:05:04.521
Pick a hook, write the post, and keep the
promise.

124
00:05:04.521 --> 00:05:06.277
Good luck, and happy posting.

